  S("NJ","S 4474",36,"committee","2026-06-18","Introduced in the Senate, Referred to Senate Commerce Committee","Establishes safety requirements for artificial intelligence companion operators.","This bill requires an operator of an artificial intelligence (AI) companion to enact user safety policies. Under the bill, an operator of an AI companion is required to provide clear and conspicuous notification to a user continuously or periodically throughout, any AI companion interaction that the user is not communicating with a human if a reasonable individual interacting with the AI companion would believe that the individual is interacting…",[],"https://www.njleg.state.nj.us/bill-search/2026/S4474",1,0);
  S("NJ","S 4701",36,"committee","2026-10-01","Introduced in the Senate, Referred to Senate Economic Growth Committee","\"GAI Accountability Act;\" imposes civil penalties on generative artificial intelligence platforms engaging in harmful activity, including exploitation of children.","This bill, known as the “GAI Accountability Act,” imposes civil liability on the owners, operators, and developers of generative artificial intelligence (GAI) platforms that facilitate certain harms against children. Under the bill, the owner, operator, or developer of any GAI platform that does business in, is based in, or operates from this State, or that is otherwise accessible to the residents of this State, is liable for a civil penalty of…",[],"https://www.njleg.state.nj.us/bill-search/2026/S4701",1,0);
  S("NJ","S 4702",36,"committee","2026-10-01","Introduced in the Senate, Referred to Senate Economic Growth Committee","\"AI Likeness Protection Act\"; concerns distributing realistic representation of individual's image, likeness, or voice created using generative artificial intelligence.","This bill prohibits the unauthorized distribution of a realistic representation of an individual using a generative artificial intelligence system. Under the bill, a “generative artificial intelligence system” or “GenAI system” is a technology system that is trained on data and can generate derived synthetic content, including text, images, video, and audio, which content emulates the structure and characteristics of the system’s training data…",[],"https://www.njleg.state.nj.us/bill-search/2026/S4702",1,0);
  S("NJ","S 4712",36,"committee","2026-10-01","Introduced in the Senate, Referred to Senate Economic Growth Committee","Imposes 10 percent tax on computer processing for certain artificial intelligence systems and dedicates revenue to \"AI Workforce Impact Transition Fund.\"","This bill imposes on AI computer processors a tax of 10 percent on the value generated by AI computer processing. The bill dedicates revenues to the support of displaced workers transitioning to an alternate career due to artificial intelligence. Under the bill, an AI computer processor is required to pay the 10 percent tax on the value generated by AI computer processing. An “AI computer processor” is an entity, including a contracted processor…",[],"https://www.njleg.state.nj.us/bill-search/2026/S4712",1,0);
  S("NJ","S 4754",36,"committee","2026-10-05","Introduced in the Senate, Referred to Senate Commerce Committee","Expand existing prohibition against unauthorized practice of various professions to include content produced by or with assistance of artificial intelligence.","This bill provides that content created by artificial intelligence is subject to the prohibitions against the unauthorized practice of a profession. Specifically, the bill provides that conduct which is prohibited the law as the unauthorized practice of a profession as determined by the Director of the Division of Consumer Affairs includes the production of content by artificial intelligence or generative artificial intelligence. Further, under…",[],"https://www.njleg.state.nj.us/bill-search/2026/S4754",1,0);
  S("NJ","S 4758",36,"committee","2026-10-05","Introduced in the Senate, Referred to Senate Commerce Committee","Requires artificial intelligence companion operators to provide notifications that users are not communicating with human.","This bill requires an operator of an artificial intelligence (AI) companion to provide clear and conspicuous notification to a user at the beginning of, and periodically throughout, any AI companion interaction that the user is not communicating with a human. The notification is to be provided either verbally or in writing. After the notification is provided at the beginning of the interaction, it is to be provided at least every three hours for…",[],"https://www.njleg.state.nj.us/bill-search/2026/S4758",1,0);
